{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1506531-enlightenments-from-non-werewolves","id":1506531,"title":"Enlightenments from Non-Werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-26T14:15:01-07:00","id":1506531,"title":"Enlightenments from Non-Werewolves","content":"Just a fun idea I had the other night. We know that Devourers can eat other werewolves in a ritualistic fashion to gain powerful effects that only last for a span of time. I was kind of wondering what it would be like if Uratha could also devour other splats, gaining even stranger abilities at the cost of weird weaknesses. Like, what happens if they consume a vampire, would they gain Impossible Regeneration at the cost of a sunlight weakness? If they eat a changeling, could they grow specific goblin fruits from their hide at the cost of being unable to lie? Stuff like that. I'm still thinking up ideas for potential enlightenments, but one thing I do want to emphasize with this concept:<br /> <br /> This is NOT an excuse to give Disciplines/Arcana/Contracts/etc to Werewolves. These weird enlightenments are supposed to be unique powers that are nonetheless connected to the type of splat they are eating. Just giving the splat-powers to the Uratha is lazy and potentially gamebreaking in a way that doesn't fit their themes. Allowing a werewolf to treat what a vampire considers to be bashing damage as such for themselves is okay, but gaining Dominate 3 is not.<br /> <br /> Universal Enlightenment:<br /> <br /> Mystical Skin-Walker: The Uratha fools any mystic senses, seeming to be the magical creature which they have devoured, rather than a werewolf. The Beasts of Vampires regard them as kin, Mages note their primal Nimbus, etc.<br /> <br /> <u>Vampire Enlightenments:</u><br /> <br /> List of Powers:<ul><li>Eternal Night: The Werewolf treats every night as if it were their auspice moon. They also reduce all penalties to see in the dark by 2.</li> <li>Frenzied Maw: The Werewolf while in Basu-Im adds their Primal Urge/2 to all Strength, Dexterity and Stamina rolls.</li> <li>Mask of Humanity: The Devourer can choose to treat the Lunacy penalty of their current form as being 2 less (Gauru -&gt; Urshul -&gt; Dalu -&gt; Hishu/Urhan). They can reflexively choose to reduce this penalty or not whenever a character rolls for Lunacy.</li> </ul><br /> All Vampire Enlightenments grant one of the following weaknesses alongside the power, once for each enlightenment:<ul><li>The Devourer suffers 1 level of aggravated damage for every hour of sunlight they stand around in.</li> <li>The Werewolf treats their Primal Urge as being 2 higher for the purposes of Basu-Im duration.</li> <li>The Uratha cannot stomach any food besides whats permitted for their feeding restriction, and must roll Stamina + Resolve to resist vomiting it back up upon consumption. They also treat their Primal Urge as 1 higher to determine the feeding restriction.</li> <li>Select 1 Vampiric Bane: The Werewolf gains that Bane as if it were a spirit Bane/Ban.</li> </ul><br /> <u>Mage Enlightenments:</u><br /> <br /> List of Powers:<ul><li>Counter-Charm: The Uratha gets a sixth sense whenever an Awakened spell is used upon them. They can spend 1 Essence to perform a Clash of Wills like a Counterspell, using Primal Urge + Wisdom instead.</li> <li>Lunacy Play: When a character fails a roll to resist Lunacy, the Uratha can spend 1 Essence to force the character to dramatically fail instead.</li> <li>Spiritkin Legacy: Select 1 Gift, except a Wolf Gift. The Uratha is treated as knowing all Facets of that Gift, and gains the rote quality on rolls to use its Facets.</li> </ul><br /> All Mage Enlightenments grant one of the following weaknesses alongside the power, once for each enlightenment:<ul><li>The Uratha's Lunacy is hideous enough to generate Paradox, which spills into the environment: If a group of characters fails a Lunacy roll, or if a single individual dramatically fails the roll, create an Abyssal Environmental Tilt.</li> <li>The Werewolf gains flashes of Active Mage Sight, which force them to roll Resolve + Composure when exposed to Mysteries of Opacity greater than Primal Urge/2. On a failure, they gain the Broken, Madness, or Obsession Condition.</li> <li>The Werewolf's sympathetic connections are unusually strong, treated as being 1 stage higher for the purposes of exploiting them.</li> </ul><br /> More to come, if I can think them up. There's also a few Uratha Enlightenments that I think could also work for other splats, but I don't have a table for that yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T16:51:27-07:00","id":1506668,"title":"","content":"So, yesterday I said that some of the Uratha Enlightenments could also work for other splats. As a purely optional addition, you can use the following table to treat related Enlightenments as one for the devoured splat, with an accompanying weakness. That might seem a bit harsh, but considering how by default an Uratha would need to consume one of their own kind to gain powers, of which there's only so many of them in the world, I think it evens out.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the weird formatting, I'm not sure the forum's table are meant to handle so many rows and columns. &quot;O&quot; is allowed, &quot;X&quot; is not allowed.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=