idth: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">X</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Sun-Chaser</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">X</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">X</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">X</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">X</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">X</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Stainless Harmony</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">X</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">X</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">X</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">O</td> </tr> </table></div> In addition, here's a few more things!<br /> <br /> <u>Changeling Enlightenments</u><br /> <br /> List of Powers:<ul><li>Dream Eater: The Uratha can eat emotions and dreams, draining Glamour like a Changeling and treating the consumed Glamour as if it were (Points Consumed - 1) points of Essence. This counts as Essence for dietary purposes.</li> <li>Fruit Hide: By spending 1 Essence, the Devourer can grow (Purity) Goblin Fruits of the same variety from their fur, so long as they have consumed that fruit before.</li> <li>Tools For the Job: The Uratha gains the Hunter's Panoply Dread Power as if they were a Huntsman.</li> </ul><br /> All Changeling Enlightenments grant one of the following weaknesses alongside the power, once for each enlightenment:<ul><li>The Werewolf treats Cold Iron as if it were silver for the purposes of damage and regeneration.</li> <li>The Werewolf cannot tell a lie, they automatically fail if they make the attempt.</li> <li>Huntsmen regard the Uratha as if they were an escaped Changeling from Arcadia.</li> </ul><u>Promethean Enlightenments</u><br /> <br /> List of Powers:<ul><li>Needless: The Uratha ignores their dietary restriction, and can sustain themselves with any organic matter they consume.</li> <li>Resuscitation: The Devourer can spend 5 Essence while touching a dead character of equal or lower Primal Urge (or equivalent Power Stat). The character is brought back to life, assuming they have not died beyond the last 24 hours.</li> <li>Storm-Clad: Electricity heals the werewolf, rather than hurts them. They regain 1 point of Essence for every 3 levels of damage healed.</li> </ul><br /> All Promethean Enlightenments grant one of the following weaknesses alongside the power, once for each enlightenment:<ul><li>Whenever the Devourer attempts a meaningful conversation with a normal human, they must first roll Primal Urge against the human's Resolve + Composure. On a <i>failure</i>, the conversation continues as normal. On a success, the conversation goes nowhere and the human attempts to leave as soon as possible.</li> <li>Essence spent by the Werewolf counts as Pyros for the purposes of Wastelands and Firestorms. They are treated as having an Azoth Rating of (Primal Urge - 2, min 0) to determine if they can be detected by Pandorans.</li> <li>Fire is treated as silver for the purposes of damage and regeneration.</li> </ul><br /> More to come, eventually. Feel free to come up with your own ideas, and let me know your thoughts on what I have thus far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}